### Clinic Appointment System - manual test flow
### Uses the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### After each login request, copy the "token" value from the response
### into the matching @xxxToken variable below, then run the requests in order.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 0. Health check (public, no token needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### =========================================================
### AUTH
### =========================================================

### 1. Register a new patient
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alex Patient",
  "email": "alex.patient@example.com",
  "password": "Patient@12345"
}


### 2. Login as the patient (paste the returned token into @patientToken below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alex.patient@example.com",
  "password": "Patient@12345"
}

### Paste patient token here
@patientToken = PASTE_PATIENT_TOKEN_HERE


### 3. Login as the seeded admin (paste the returned token into @adminToken below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}

### Paste admin token here
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE


### =========================================================
### SERVICES (main entity) - admin manages, both roles can view
### =========================================================

### 4. Patient/Admin: list services (empty at first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/services
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}


### 5. Admin: create a service
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "General Consultation",
  "description": "Standard GP consultation",
  "durationMinutes": 30
}

### Paste the created service's "id" here for the requests below
@serviceId = PASTE_SERVICE_ID_HERE


### 6. Patient trying to create a service should be blocked (expect 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/services
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should Fail",
  "description": "Patients cannot create services",
  "durationMinutes": 15
}


### 7. Admin: update the service
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "General Consultation",
  "description": "Standard GP consultation - 30 minutes",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "active": true
}


### =========================================================
### APPOINTMENTS (action/transaction entity)
### =========================================================

### 8. Patient: book an appointment (future date required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "appointmentDateTime": "2026-09-01T10:00:00",
  "notes": "First visit"
}

### Paste the created appointment's "id" here
@appointmentId = PASTE_APPOINTMENT_ID_HERE


### 9. Business rule check: booking the SAME slot again should fail (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "appointmentDateTime": "2026-09-01T10:00:00",
  "notes": "Should be rejected - slot already booked"
}


### 10. Business rule check: booking a PAST date should fail (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "appointmentDateTime": "2020-01-01T10:00:00",
  "notes": "Should be rejected - in the past"
}


### 11. Patient: view own appointments ("My Records")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments/me
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}


### 12. Patient trying to list ALL appointments should be blocked (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}


### 13. Admin: view all appointments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 14. Admin: confirm the appointment
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments/{{appointmentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}


### 15. Patient: cancel their own appointment
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments/{{appointmentId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}


### 16. Business rule check: the same slot can now be re-booked (cancelling freed it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "appointmentDateTime": "2026-09-01T10:00:00",
  "notes": "Re-booking the freed slot"
}


### 17. Admin: deactivate the service (soft delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 18. Booking a now-inactive service should fail (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{patientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "appointmentDateTime": "2026-09-02T10:00:00",
  "notes": "Should be rejected - service inactive"
}
